action as speculative.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"target_molecule\": \"L-Proline\",\n  \"overall_strategy\": \"Construct an evidence-graded network containing ten distinct reaction sequences, not ten independently demonstrated prebiotic syntheses. P1 follows the reported cyanosulfidic construction of the proline aminonitrile, followed by chemically expected but unquantified hydrolysis. P2-P8 are explicitly speculative mechanistic alternatives involving nitrile reduction, sulfurization, cyclization, or sulfur-assisted hydrolysis. P9-P10 explore a glutamate/P5C route and contain an explicitly unresolved carboxylate-reduction step; they are research hypotheses, not established syntheses. Small C2/C3 keto acids are supplied feedstocks for those two paths, not claimed products of CO2 fixation. All achiral routes produce L-proline together with D-proline; separate stereoisomer nodes prevent a racemate from being mislabeled as enantiopure L-proline. This network therefore reaches L-proline as a racemate component, not isolated or selectively synthesized L-proline. No demonstrated prebiotic resolution step is supplied: proline phase amplification requires an initial bias, and the strongest reported enrichment used non-prebiotic chloroform (Klussmann et al., 2006). Conditions are proposed geological operating windows unless explicitly identified as experimental observations; detailed Patel et al. procedures were not independently verified from their supplementary information. Neutral formulas represent acid-base reference species. S8 is an idealized endpoint for oxidized sulfur, not a claim that every photoreaction exclusively produces molecular S8. Null formation environments indicate supplied feedstocks or species formed in multiple environments. No oxygen, enzymes, or unsupported mineral catalysts are assumed. Detection-only discharge and extraterrestrial results are not converted into invented intermediate-resolved reactions.\",\n  \"molecules\": [\n    {\n      \"id\":