rg/journals/microbiology/articles/10.3389/fmicb.2021.793664/full\n  50. (PDF) Hydrothermal Degradation of Amino Acids - https://www.researchgate.net/publication/354487413_Hydrothermal_Degradation_of_Amino_Acids\n  51. Spectroscopy of Hydrothermal Reactions 25: Kinetics of the Decarboxylation of Protein Amino Acids and the Effect of Side Chains on Hydrothermal Stability - https://www.researchgate.net/publication/231633952_Spectroscopy_of_Hydrothermal_Reactions_25_Kinetics_of_the_Decarboxylation_of_Protein_Amino_Acids_and_the_Effect_of_Side_Chains_on_Hydrothermal_Stability\n  52. Alanine enantiomers in the Murchison meteorite - https://www.nature.com/articles/28306\n  53. Non-racemic amino acids in the Murray and Murchison meteorites - ScienceDirect - https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S001670379900280X\n  54. Parity-Violating Energy Shifts of Murchison L-Amino Acids are Consistent with an Electroweak Origin of Meteorite L-Enantiomeric Excesses - https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11084-009-9162-9\n  55. Enrichment of the amino acid l-isovaline by aqueous alteration on CI and CM meteorite parent bodies - https://www.pnas.org/doi/full/10.1073/pnas.0811618106\n  56. Homochirality: a prerequisite or consequence of life? - https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.12850\n  57. The science from asteroid sample return missions - https://arxiv.org/pdf/2604.22182\n  58. OSIRIS-REx Returned a Pristine Sample of Asteroid Bennu: Takeaways from the Mission's Contamination Control and Knowledge Program - https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.12249\n  59. ENANTIOMERIC EXCESSES INDUCED IN AMINO ACIDS BY ULTRAVIOLET CIRCULARLY POLARIZED LIGHT IRRADIATION OF EXTRATERRESTRIAL ICE ANALOGS: A POSSIBLE SOURCE OF ASYMMETRY FOR PREBIOTIC CHEMISTRY - IOPscience - https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/0004-637X/788/1/79\n  60. Shaping light in 3D for direct asymmetric photochemistry: a 1000-fold enantioselectivity enhancement - https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-77096-w\n  61. T