", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_002", "mol_007", "mol_014"]}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "name": "Carbide-derived acetylene with externally supplied HCN", "description": "Uses calcium carbide hydrolysis for acetylene, followed by gas delivery into the copper-containing, sulfide-poor source pool. The hydrolysis chemistry is established, but natural carbide inventory and acetylene recovery are not. The common finishing hydrolyses remain unquantified.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_014", "rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_002", "mol_012", "mol_014"]}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "name": "Methane-ammonia HCN supply combined with methane-discharge acetylene supply", "description": "Combines two discharge source channels before convergence at hydrocyanation. The first two listed reactions are parallel feedstock-generation branches, not a claim that one consumes the other's products. Simultaneous useful HCN and acetylene inventories must be measured; no paired source yield is inferred.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_011", "rxn_013", "rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_001", "mol_002", "mol_007", "mol_014"]}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "name": "Methane-nitrogen HCN supply combined with methane-discharge acetylene supply", "description": "Combines the conditional CH4/N2 HCN source and methane-to-acetylene source as parallel branches feeding rxn_001. Additional ammonia and sulfide are supplied to the aqueous sequence. This variant has two unquantified source channels and does not improve evidence for the shared proline hydrolysis endpoint.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_012", "rxn_013", "rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_001", "mol_002", "mol_008", "mol_014"]}, {"pathway_id": "P8", "name": "Methane-ammonia HCN supply combined with carbide-derived acetylene", "description": "Joins discharge-derived HCN and carbide-derived acetylene at the sulfide-poor copper stage. The source branches can be geographically separate because their transported products are the simple feedstocks rather than the reactive aldehyde or imine. Their capture efficiencies and delivery timing remain unmeasured.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_011", "rxn_014", "rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_001", "mol_002", "mol_012", "mol_014"]}, {"pathway_id": "P9", "name": "Methane-nitrogen HCN supply combined with carbide-derived acetylene", "description": "Combines a nitrogen-activation-dependent HCN source with carbide hydrolysis. Both source modules must supply measurable feedstock flux before the common backbone is considered viable. The network does not infer natural carbide abundance or successful proline formation from a favorable bulk energy balance.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_012", "rxn_014", "rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_001", "mol_002", "mol_007", "mol_014"]}, {"pathway_id": "P10", "name": "Direct simple feedstocks with copper-assisted C3 nitrile photoreduction", "description": "A process variant of P1 replacing rxn_003 with the copper-assisted alternative rxn_015. It is conditional on demonstrated catalyst survival and acceleration in the actual cyanide-sulfide mixture. It is not counted as an independently established proline-skeleton mechanism or evidence for enantioselectivity.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_015", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_009", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008", "mol_009", "mol_012", "mol_014"]}], "hub_molecules": ["mol_001", "mol_002", "mol_003", "mol_004", "mol_005", "mol_006", "mol_00